    "Description": "Red Hat JBoss Core Services is a set of supplementary software for Red Hat JBoss middleware products. This software, such as Apache HTTP Server, is common to multiple JBoss middleware products and packaged under Red Hat JBoss Core Services, to allow for faster distribution of updates and for a more consistent update experience.\n\nThis release of Red Hat JBoss Core Services Apache HTTP Server 2.4.62 serves as a replacement for Red Hat JBoss Core Services Apache HTTP Server 2.4.57 Service Pack 6, and includes bug fixes and enhancements, which are documented in the Release Notes linked to in the References section.\n\nSecurity Fix(es):\n\n* httpd: HTTP Response Splitting in multiple modules (CVE-2024-24795)\n* mod_http2: DoS by null pointer in websocket over HTTP/2 (CVE-2024-36387)\n* openssl: SSL_select_next_proto buffer overread (CVE-2024-5535)\n\nFor more details about the security issue(s), including the impact, a CVSS score, acknowledgments, and other related information, refer to the CVE page(s) listed in the References section.",
